If it's possible to dig down (>) and go through the floor, why isn't possible
to dig up (<) and go through the ceiling when levitating? If you try this,
nethack tells you you can't reach the ceiling; however, when you quaff
a cursed potion of levitation you bump your head on the ceiling, so it
*should* be possible... Things could be made more interesting by having
boulders fall on your head when digging up... Digging up would be useful
when trying to get out with the Amulet without mapping all these boring
maze levels of Hell...

If, like me, you like to polypile, you probably already know this, but
here are some steady sources of supplies for polymorphing:
- gems can be obtained by polymorphing stacks of rocks
- arrow and dart traps are steady sources of weapons
- nymphs are steady sources of potions
- rob a shop and get an infinite supply of cream pies from Keystone Kops;
  they polymorph nicely into goodies (I once got 16 tins of spinach and
  10 tins of wraith meat that way!!!!)
- polymorphing boulders into statues gives a good chance of getting
  spellbooks (hidden in the statues; just pick-axe them to pieces)
- get all these whistles and empty boxes and polymorph them into useful
  things like blindfolds and stethoscopes...
- the best supply of armor is a military barracks, but you have to be
  pretty good or have a ring of conflict to get past that one... Otherwise
  go get all these colorful hooded cloaks and pairs of hard shoes...
- there is no good supply of wands, unless you found the right shop, but who
  needs wands anyway when you can get lots of spellbooks from polymorphing
  boulders??? (except for wands of polymorph, of course; always take those
  out of the pile!!!)
- rings can be gotten also from military barracks, or sinks
- as far as I know, there are no good tricks to get scrolls or amulets in
  quantity; you have to rely on shops, monsters carrying them or Vlad's
  tower...

Polypiling requires only patience, but it's the best way to prepare your
character for the trip to Hell... Of course, you need a wand or spellbook
of polymorph to start with...

